\section*{Data Availability Statement}

The IEA Hydrogen Projects Database (March 2024 release) is published by the International Energy Agency at \url{https://www.iea.org/data-and-statistics/data-product/hydrogen-projects-database} under a CC BY-NC-SA license; researchers can download the publicly available version directly. All time-varying macro covariates are constructed from public sources: ICAP for EU ETS allowance prices, ICE Endex for TTF gas futures, ENTSO-E Transparency Platform for day-ahead electricity prices, CBOE for the VIX, Baker-Bloom-Davis for the Economic Policy Uncertainty index, FRED for US interest rates and exchange rates, and Yahoo Finance via the \texttt{yfinance} library for hydrogen-sector equity prices. The processed person-period panel and all analysis code (Python and R) used to produce the results in this paper are available at:

\begin{center}
\url{https://github.com/sakesaakstra/blueCCS-hydrogen}
\end{center}

The repository includes complete replication instructions, locked dependency versions (\texttt{requirements.txt} for Python, \texttt{renv.lock} for R), and a \texttt{CITATION.cff} file. See Appendix~B for a detailed list of data sources.

